  'saccular aneurysm' => 'A rounded pouch protruding from one side of an artery because of focal wall weakness, with rupture and clot formation risks determined by location, size, and growth.',
  'sacral region' => 'The lower back and posterior pelvic region overlying the sacrum, a fused triangular bone that connects the lumbar spine with the pelvis.',
  'sacral vertebra' => 'One of the fused vertebrae forming the sacrum, which supports the spine, joins the pelvic bones, and transmits trunk weight to the lower limbs.',
  'sacrococcygeal teratoma' => 'A congenital tumor arising at the base of the spine and containing tissues from multiple germ layers; large fetal lesions can cause high-output heart failure or hydrops.',
